  <data name="LeAudio_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>LE Audio (LC3) connection (experimental)</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_Summary.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Lets Windows connect these earbuds over LE Audio with the LC3 codec instead of Classic Bluetooth A2DP. Your PC's Bluetooth must support LE Audio.</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_Switch" xml:space="preserve"><value>Switch to LE Audio</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_Restore" xml:space="preserve"><value>Restore Classic Bluetooth</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_StatusLe" xml:space="preserve"><value>Current: LE Audio (LC3), both earbuds paired.</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_StatusLeSingle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Current: LE Audio, but only one earbud is paired, so sound may play on one side only. Switch again to fix it.</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_StatusClassic" xml:space="preserve"><value>Current: Classic Bluetooth (A2DP).</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_StatusUnpaired" xml:space="preserve"><value>Current: these earbuds are not paired with this PC.</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_ConfirmTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Change how the earbuds connect?</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_ConfirmSwitch" xml:space="preserve"><value>When asked, put the earbuds in the case, open the lid and hold the case button to enter pairing mode. Once pairing mode is detected, EncoDeck removes this PC's old pairing with the earbuds (your phone and other devices are not affected) and pairs both earbuds over LE Audio automatically; audio stops meanwhile.

Afterwards Windows lists two entries with the same name (one is the other earbud), and audio plays through "Speakers (earbud name)".</value></data>
  <data name="LeAudio_ConfirmRestore" xml:space="preserve"><value>EncoDeck will remove this PC's LE Audio and associated Classic Bluetooth pairings; audio will stop. After cleanup, put the earbuds in pairing mode and manually pair them using Add device in Windows Bluetooth settings.</value></data>
